1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
In this video, we're going to be talking about some more physical safety features with the laser.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000
So in addition to using approved materials, there are a couple other safety things we're going to ask of you.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The first and most important is that you are required to remain with the laser the entire time it is running.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,000
So if the laser is cutting, scoring, or engraving, if the laser is running one of your designs, you are required to be with the laser.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
And to define that a little more, we want you within arm's reach and where you can see inside of the laser.

6
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,000
So it's okay if you're standing here on your cell phone, if you're making your next design using the computer.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
We're not saying you have to be here staring into it the entire time.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
But we do want you within arm's reach so you can notice if something goes wrong.

9
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
And we don't want you on the other side of the room chatting with your buddy, or getting ready with your next sewing design,

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,000
or whatever else you might be working on.

11
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:04,310
Up at the top of the laser, we have our start stop button.

12
00:01:04,310 --> 00:01:09,310
We want you to monitor the laser, and there is never any harm in pausing a design while it's running.

13
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:16,310
So if you're ever concerned, you see something that looks like it might be an issue, you see some sort of small flame,

14
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:22,310
it's entirely okay to just pause the laser and give it a minute and see what happens.

15
00:01:22,310 --> 00:01:31,310
And that's part of why we want you as close as we do it, so that you can reach over and just pause the laser if something looks like it's going wrong.

16
00:01:31,310 --> 00:01:38,310
If something has gone very wrong, we do have an emergency stop button back here in the corner.

17
00:01:38,310 --> 00:01:44,310
That's going to be most useful for things like the laser arm has gotten itself stuck, it's trying to move and can't.

18
00:01:44,310 --> 00:01:47,310
You hear what sounds like breaking components.

19
00:01:47,310 --> 00:01:52,310
You see some amount of smoke that you're really concerned about.

20
00:01:52,310 --> 00:02:02,310
At this point, I do want to specify any sort of laser cutting, engraving, scoring, any use of the laser is going to produce some amount of smoke and sometimes small flames,

21
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:05,310
and that is to be expected.

22
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:12,310
Laser cutting is the process of burning away material, so you do sometimes get small flames and things like that.

23
00:02:12,310 --> 00:02:17,310
What we want to be concerned about is if those small flames start to turn into larger flames,

24
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:22,310
if the laser moves onto a different part of your design and part of your design is still on fire.

25
00:02:22,310 --> 00:02:30,310
That is when we want to be concerned and start thinking about hitting either the pause button or the emergency stop button.

26
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:37,310
I tend to default to the pause button first because you can recover your design, you can keep going.

27
00:02:37,310 --> 00:02:43,310
So if the flame sort of blows itself out because of the air movement from the filter, you're good to keep going.

28
00:02:43,310 --> 00:02:51,310
If you hit the emergency stop button, it turns off the power to the laser, and you will not be able to recover your design.

29
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:57,310
So you want to always start with the pause button first, unless you're like,

30
00:02:57,310 --> 00:03:04,310
oh, this something has gone just catastrophically wrong, in which case go straight to the emergency stop button.

31
00:03:04,310 --> 00:03:09,310
Along with the emergency stop button, we have one other really nice safety feature.

32
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:12,310
That is this box right here.

33
00:03:12,310 --> 00:03:16,310
This box is our fire suppression tool.

34
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:21,310
So it is actively monitoring the inside of the laser any time the laser is on.

35
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:25,310
It will make noise if it detects smoke and flame.

36
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:30,310
And if it detects an excessive amount of smoke and flame, it will begin to sound like a fire alarm.

37
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:33,310
It will begin to make sort of a whooping sound.

38
00:03:33,310 --> 00:03:40,310
It is loud. It is loud because it wants you and others to be aware that something has gone wrong.

39
00:03:40,310 --> 00:03:43,310
When it goes off, it will do several things.

40
00:03:43,310 --> 00:03:53,310
It will turn off power to the laser again, and it will also spray CO2 gas from this box into the laser itself.

41
00:03:53,310 --> 00:04:01,310
So if you hear this box start to whoop like a fire alarm, what we want you to do is nothing.

42
00:04:01,310 --> 00:04:10,310
We don't want you to rush over and open the lid because we want this box to be able to spray the CO2 gas into the laser first.

43
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:14,310
What we do want you to do is make sure staff are aware.

44
00:04:14,310 --> 00:04:16,310
They should be because it is going to be pretty loud.

45
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:20,310
But if they are not, wave over a staff member, say, hey, it is making a bunch of noise,

46
00:04:20,310 --> 00:04:23,310
and then await staff instructions.

47
00:04:23,310 --> 00:04:26,310
So we don't want you to rush over and open the lid.

48
00:04:26,310 --> 00:04:29,310
We don't want you to start rushing out of the building yelling fire.

49
00:04:29,310 --> 00:04:31,310
There is no need to panic.

50
00:04:31,310 --> 00:04:37,310
We do want you to make sure that staff are aware and follow their instructions from there.

51
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:44,310
In the event that the CO2 gas from our fire suppression box is insufficient,

52
00:04:44,310 --> 00:04:50,310
on the other side of the laser, we do have a fire blanket and fire extinguisher,

53
00:04:50,310 --> 00:04:53,310
and those will be used at staff instructions.

54
00:04:53,310 --> 00:04:59,310
So if staff say, that didn't work, the laser is still on fire, we will move to the next level of suppression.

55
00:04:59,310 --> 00:05:08,310
But we really want to let this box go first because this is a lot easier and a lot less mess to clean up.

56
00:05:08,310 --> 00:05:13,310
So hopefully none of those things end up being necessary.

57
00:05:13,310 --> 00:05:15,310
We haven't had to use them yet.

58
00:05:15,310 --> 00:05:22,310
And if you use approved materials and follow some general safety guidelines, you should be in good shape.

59
00:05:22,310 --> 00:05:29,310
And hopefully we'll never have to use any of that, but it's good information to have.

60
00:05:29,310 --> 00:05:32,310
In the next video, we'll talk about the software side of things.

61
00:05:32,310 --> 00:05:37,310
So we'll talk about Extool Studio and setting up your designs.
